\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Pairwise comparison of the original Pb--Pb dates of Table~\ref {tab:desch} with Al--Mg (panel~a), Mn--Cr (panel~b) and Hf--W (panel~c) dates for the same, rapidly cooled meteorites. The 1:1 lines were obtained using the optimal ${O}$-values (Equation~\ref {eq:A}). All three datasets are overdispersed around this line with respect to the analytical uncertainties (MSWD$\,\gg \,1$). $\omega $-values are the estimated standard deviations of the excess dispersion, assuming normality (Section~\ref {sec:discussion}). This dispersion can either be attributed to the Pb--Pb data, or to the initial $({}^{26}\mbox  {Al}/{}^{27}\mbox  {Al})_{\rm  SS}$, $({}^{53}\mbox  {Mn}/{}^{55}\mbox  {Mn})_{\rm  SS}$ or $({}^{182}\mbox  {Hf}/{}^{180}\mbox  {Hf})_{\rm  SS}$-values, or a combination. Uncertainties are reported as standard errors.}}{6}{}\protected@file@percent }
